# WHY EACH NON-OBVIOUS FLAG:
#   --wheel_scale         47.0 x scale is the rad/s at |action|=1, and the wheels
#                         TOP OUT AT 23.6. At 1.4, 81% of ticks clipped, the
#                         wheels reproduced 14% of the commanded variation, and
#                         the robot tipped over its own wheels at the riser.
#                         0.5 maps the action range exactly onto the actuator.
#   --max_wheel_diff 0    ties the wheels. The policy's differential head carries
#                         a large constant bias (action_1 mean +0.77 with the
#                         goal 0.1 deg off the nose) and pivots forever.
#   --servo_scale 1.0     the attitude hold computes the angle that puts thrust
#                         vertical; servo_scale MULTIPLIES it. At 1.5 it commands
